hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15749","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, he said: Mu'awiyah entered upon his uncle Abu Hashim ibn Utbah visiting him sick. He said: He wept. He said: Mu'awiyah said to him: What makes you weep, O uncle, is it pain distressing you, or greed for the world? He said: He said: Neither, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted us, saying: O Abu Hashim, perhaps you will attain wealth not attained by peoples, and sufficient for you of amassing wealth is a servant and a mount in the path of Allah, blessed and exalted is He. And I see that I have amassed."
"15750","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, he said: Mu'awiyah entered upon Abu Hashim ibn Utbah while he was sick weeping, and he mentioned its meaning."
